    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A defensive pact of three Alpine valleys in 1291 grew into a league of thirteen cantons by 1513.</li><li>Swiss <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pike">pikemen</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> and Burgundian armies and served as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>'s most sought-after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a>.</li><li>Without a central government, it relied on a consensus <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tagsatzung">Diet</a>; French invasion in 1798 replaced it with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/helvetic-republic">Helvetic Republic</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federal-charter-of-1291">Federal Charter of 1291</a> became the official founding document only in the 1890s, when 1 August was chosen as the Swiss national day.</p></aside>
    </section>

